00:24:37.230 --> 00:24:53.830
<v Alex Edelman>And you never know when Hanukkah is, because the calendars-- sometimes it's in early December. Sometimes it's in, like, late July. You never [BLEEP] know. But my non-Jewish friends are always like, well, you guys are lucky. You get eight days of gifts. I have never met a single Jew who has ever received eight days of gifts.
<v Alex Edelman>而且你永远不知道光明节什么时候到来，因为日历的原因——有时在十二月初，有时在七月底。你永远不知道。但我的非犹太朋友总是说：“嘿，你们真幸运，有八天的礼物。”我从来没见过哪个犹太人真的收到过八天的礼物。

